### Architecture Overview: GatedDeltaNet

This layer replaces the standard Key-Value (KV) cache found in standard attention mechanisms with a **recurrent state mechanism** that operates per value head.

#### 1. Core Mechanism
Instead of storing static KV pairs for every position, the layer maintains a dynamic **recurrent state** ($s_t$) for each value head.

*   **State Decay**: At every position $t$, the state decays by a learned factor ($\alpha$). This prevents the state from accumulating irrelevant information over long sequences without regularization.
    $$s_t = \alpha \cdot s_{t-1}$$
